'''Sahloknir''' is a leveled [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragon]] brought back from the grave by [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin]] east of [[Skyrim:Kynesgrove|Kynesgrove]]. Depending on what type of dragon he is, he can breathe either [[Skyrim:Fire Breath|fire]] or [[Skyrim:Frost Breath|frost]].

Sah Lok Nir translates to "Phantom Sky Hunt".
{{NewLeft}}

==Related Quests==
* {{Quest Link|A Blade in the Dark}}

==Dialogue==

When you fight him during the quest [[Skyrim:A Blade in the Dark|A Blade in the Dark]] he will use the following lines in combat:

*''"I am Sahloknir! Hear my Voice and despair!"''

*''"{{sic|Thurri|Thuri}} {{hover|My lord (will) devour your souls in Sovngarde!|du hin sille ko Sovngarde!}}"''

*''"Your Voice is strong ... for a mortal."''

*''"{{sic|Dohaviin|Dovahkiin}}, your Voice is no match for mine!"''

*''"My lord Alduin requires your death. I am glad to oblige him."''

*''"My Voice has been silent for too long!"''

*''"I see that mortals have become arrogant while I slept."''

*''"It's to be a real fight, then. Good!"'' (if health is low)

*''"Hiding will not save you!"'' (if you are trying to hide)

If spoken to, he uses the same line of dialogue as other named dragons who have yet to be resurrected from a burial mound by [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin]]: ''"Speak, if you have aught to say worth the listening."''

==Notes==
*He is unaffected by the [[Skyrim:Bend Will|Bend Will]] shout and cannot be [[Skyrim:Dragon Riding|ridden]].
*If [[Skyrim:Miraak|Miraak]] steals his soul during [[Skyrim:A Blade in the Dark|A Blade in the Dark]], [[Skyrim:Delphine|Delphine]] will still give you credit.

